WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:06.120
Known as "The God of Lightning," Hajime Kashimo&nbsp;
has returned after four hundred years of abject&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:11.880
silence to exact vengeance upon one specific&nbsp;
man. This isn't any ordinary, bottom of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:17.440
barrel Miwa level slop of a character. Hajime&nbsp;
Kashimo was undoubtedly the strongest man of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.720
his time and someone Kenjaku specifically&nbsp;
sought out to be apart of his culling game.

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.360
However, Sukuna never existed&nbsp;
in that time and perfection was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.320
unattainable for Hajime. Now given&nbsp;
the chance at redemption its time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.480
to witness what it means to have&nbsp;
perfected the use of curse energy.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.200
Turning and seeing someone&nbsp;
approaching him at a high speed now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:40.320
Sukuna tells them that he&nbsp;
better not let them down!

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.840
Flashing into the sky we see that&nbsp;
without any time for anyone to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.920
mourn or feel sorrow for Gojo's death,&nbsp;
the one that came in to take his place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:53.349
against the KING OF CURSES, WAS NO OTHER&nbsp;
THAN, THE THUNDER GOD, HAJIME KASHIMO!!

00:00:53.349 --> 00:00:53.360
Chapter 237

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.840
Hovering 203 meters off the ground,&nbsp;
Kashimo himself is surprised when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.840
notices an object falling from even&nbsp;
further up. Atop that meteor-sized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.080
piece of ice was none other than&nbsp;
the frozen queen herself, Uraume!

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:10.040
Getting surprised herself, above Uraume appeared&nbsp;
Hakari, yelling out that she won't be going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.000
anywhere. Not interested at all in taking on the&nbsp;
special grade sorcerer, Uraume prepares her ice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:21.000
formation, while simultaneously Hakari pulls up&nbsp;
his hands and activates his Domain Expansion.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.560
Even though Hakari was able to trap the ice queen&nbsp;
within his own domain, the large block of ice that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.720
she stood on kept plummeting towards the earth&nbsp;
below. Down below, of course, was none other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:35.480
than the king of curses who began extending&nbsp;
his hand towards the now melting iceberg.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:40.680
Now, like a torrential ocean wave, all of the ice&nbsp;
melts into water under an endothermic reaction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:45.640
allowing the one-handed demon to grab a&nbsp;
certain object. So, remember back to when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:51.880
Yorozu tried to show Sukuna love but failed.&nbsp;
Well, in the end, and in a similar way to Mai,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:57.320
she used her innate technique creation to use her&nbsp;
remaining cursed energy to create a certain item.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.720
Now with this dagger-like item clenched firmly&nbsp;
in the hand of the one she used to love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.920
it's revealed that what Yorozu created&nbsp;
was a replica of an ancient item Sukuna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.960
used to wield. The cursed tool Kamutoke. This&nbsp;
tool's ability seems to be one that allows the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.840
user to control some form of electricity.&nbsp;
Within milliseconds of receiving the tool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.280
Sukuna launches a blast towards his opponent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:23.280
which hilariously enough is perfectly countered&nbsp;
by the effects of Kashimo’s own curse energy.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.640
Speaking up now, Kashimo asks the king of curses&nbsp;
if he earned the title of the strongest or was he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:34.360
simply born with unbeatable prowess. Not actually&nbsp;
having a clue himself, Sukuna answers that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:40.920
can't say much, but what he can say is that&nbsp;
he was born cursed, an unwanted little wretch.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:48.000
Stopping myself for a moment, this really makes&nbsp;
me question if he was born of a human and cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:55.560
spirit, possibly in a similar way to that of Choso&nbsp;
or even Yuji. Was he useless at birth like Toji,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:01.520
Mai, and Maki and underwent a heavenly restriction&nbsp;
to greatly increase his physical capabilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:07.480
then somehow re-entered the world&nbsp;
of Jujutsu? From this, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:12.760
it's obvious that he was an outcast&nbsp;
from birth, an unwanted little wretch.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:18.320
For those curious about a major part of what&nbsp;
Jujutsu Kaisen is about, it is all about teaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:24.640
people what love is. It sounds soppy and cringe,&nbsp;
but it's this underlying part of the story that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:29.000
now with a lot of the most loved characters&nbsp;
beginning to fall or having fallen, is making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:36.640
itself even more apparent. To me, Sukuna fears&nbsp;
death because he is the strongest. He thinks you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:42.880
are alone in death, which also is crazy after what&nbsp;
happened recently. We saw that in Jujutsu Kaisen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:49.480
when you die, you aren't alone; you are surrounded&nbsp;
by all of your loved ones, be it in this world or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:54.720
the next, human or cursed spirit. Jogo upon&nbsp;
death instantly found his close friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:04:00.160
and so did Gojo with his entire year from school;&nbsp;
even freaking Toji was there. I don't know, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.960
people are gonna find it weird, and it depends on&nbsp;
how Yuji talk-no-jutsu’s it, but the story began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:10.640
with Yuji being taught what love is, and it's&nbsp;
probably going to end with him teaching Sukuna.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.600
Enough of me talking about love though; it's time&nbsp;
for Kashimo to attempt it. Still in conversation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.600
he asks how Sukuna is able to connect with others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:29.360
how can he love those beneath him without&nbsp;
knowing some kind of weakness. To Kashimo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.200
it's something he just can't comprehend. He&nbsp;
was always surrounded by the most feeble and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:39.800
pathetic people, no more than dirt in the eyes of&nbsp;
cursed energy or pebbles of sand on a beach. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:45.040
an attempt to understand, he pleads with Sukuna&nbsp;
to enlighten him. Is strength itself solitude,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:50.320
or is the endless search for greater power&nbsp;
simply a burden the strong have to bear alone?

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:55.960
Amused with just how greedy Kashimo is for&nbsp;
information on who he was, Sukuna chuckles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:01.240
but lets him know that he’ll teach him, so be&nbsp;
sure to give him his best shot. Absolutely stoked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.360
with the chance of a lifetime and something he&nbsp;
personally has wanted for hundreds of years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:10.480
Kashimo bursts forth. Jumping up,&nbsp;
he slams his staff down atop Sukuna,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:15.400
only for him to comfortably block with an electric&nbsp;
burst before darting out of striking range.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:20.320
Activating his one-time-use innate technique,&nbsp;
Kashimo releases his awed-over Mythic Beast:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:25.400
Amber and proceeds to sock a shocked Sukuna with&nbsp;
a flurry of punches, sending him sliding back.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.640
Warping his body into an otherworldly form,&nbsp;
Kashimo directs his face at his opponent and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:34.400
sends a blast of electricity that explodes&nbsp;
upon contact with him. Joking that this form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:39.480
of his is far too loud, it's explained that&nbsp;
Mythic Beast Amber transforms Kashimo’s body&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:43.840
into something else. I kind of think of&nbsp;
it like Ino’s Auspicious Beast Technique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:48.760
but instead of being an intermediary, Kashimo&nbsp;
literally becomes one of these Mythic beasts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.400
warping his body with cursed energy&nbsp;
to resemble it, in this example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:57.560
the Amber version. During the time this ability&nbsp;
is active, Kashimo can use any phenomena that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:02.840
can be created by electricity until his cursed&nbsp;
energy runs out. I just want to mention that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:08.800
this means it's possible Kashimo can travel at 90&nbsp;
percent the speed of light or over 250,000 km/s.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.160
Using this speed increase to his advantage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.440
Kashimo takes Sukuna somewhat by surprise&nbsp;
and sends a blast of sonic electricity into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.760
the ground directly below him. Instantly&nbsp;
following this, Kashimo throws a fat right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:27.560
hook, connecting with Sukuna’s face,&nbsp;
leaving him flattened upon the ground.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.240
It's explained that by activating this technique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.040
Kashimo’s agility increases. He can optimize&nbsp;
the sound and tune out incorrect noises to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:40.240
match natural frequencies. If any object&nbsp;
is sent at him, it's quickly vaporized due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:45.520
to the electromagnetic waves flowing off his&nbsp;
body. Yet, once this technique concludes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:51.600
because of how badly Kashimo’s body is being&nbsp;
exerted, he will crumble to dust and die.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:56.120
Using an effect of his own cursed energy and&nbsp;
having placed a positive charge on Sukuna when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.120 --> 00:07:00.040
he hit him, Kashimo releases the negative&nbsp;
one and sends a current of electricity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:04.760
that instantaneously connects with the&nbsp;
king of curses' already weakened body.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:09.440
Apart from the reverse cursed technique, Sukuna&nbsp;
has a secret method of restoring his original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:15.760
body. One that he isn't able to abuse and can&nbsp;
only use a single time. A certain method that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:20.840
he had been intentionally waiting to use,&nbsp;
SINCE THE BEGINNING! This method was, like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:26.400
the other members of the culling game, resuming&nbsp;
his transformation through means of incarnation!

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:30.600
Activating his X-Ray vision, Kashimo is&nbsp;
able to analyze the slowly approaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:35.600
demon. Without a doubt, what stood&nbsp;
in front of him was perfection.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:39.840
When it comes to just how broken Sukuna&nbsp;
actually is, everyone needs to realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:44.320
that the reason he has extra body parts&nbsp;
and possibly internal organs is so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:49.080
his hands remain uninhibited. Then, while&nbsp;
performing a chant, his lungs remain free,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:54.280
and his heart isn't burdened by the added effects.&nbsp;
All of these extra body parts provide Sukuna with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:59.400
an immense advantage over anyone else. He may&nbsp;
be physically deformed, but that doesn't matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:04.640
or impede him in the slightest. Instead, as&nbsp;
I've mentioned, it adds to his potential.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:08.520
During the Heian period, Sukuna was armed&nbsp;
with both his incredible strength and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:13.760
cursed tools known as Supreme Martial&nbsp;
Solution and Hiten. Hiten is supposedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:21.360
the large trident-like staff that he wields,&nbsp;
whereas the Kamutoke that Yorozu created is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.000
most likely the recreation of&nbsp;
the Supreme Martial Solution.

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:30.160
With these items, Sukuna annihilated The&nbsp;
Sun, Moon, and Stars squad and the five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:34.920
void generals that served as guards to the&nbsp;
northern Fujiwara clan. Then, on top of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:40.680
he decisively defeated the Abe clan's&nbsp;
elite forces, which included Angels and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:45.640
Desshi Pacification Squad, who themselves&nbsp;
were composed of Sugawara clan members.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:49.960
Utterly blown away with the unreal achievements&nbsp;
Sukuna was able to complete over his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:55.000
Kashimo can only fawn over how beautiful&nbsp;
the demon king's true form seems.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:59.520
Taking the offensive himself now, Sukuna rushes&nbsp;
Kashimo and manages to land a double right handed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:04.240
body strike that launches the sorcerer up into&nbsp;
the sky. Using the height to his advantage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:09.680
Kashimo shoots a blast of condensed electricity&nbsp;
directly at his foe. Unconcerned, Sukuna with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:14.080
second mouth begins chanting, while simultaneously&nbsp;
telling Kashimo that he should probably dodge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:19.440
this strike. Out of nowhere, Dismantle is sent&nbsp;
forth and manages to slice the palm of Kashimo’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:23.760
improved mythic beast form. Instantly, the&nbsp;
special grade sorcerer realizes that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:29.520
is the same ability that was able to finish Gojo&nbsp;
off, as it was a slash that cut the world itself.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:35.040
Standing there, absolutely JACKED out of his mind,&nbsp;
Sukuna jokes that a fool once tried to teach him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:41.040
about love. Yet, she didn't even know what love&nbsp;
was and was also insanely lonely. Sukuna explains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:46.240
that he understood what she was trying to say;&nbsp;
however, she just had the wrong guy. In his eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:50.440
she'd have had more luck preaching her love&nbsp;
to someone like Kashimo or Gojo. It's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:54.880
that they didn't know what love was; it was&nbsp;
more that they were unable to understand it.

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:59.920
Completely confused with what he was&nbsp;
trying to say, Kashimo queries him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:05.480
only for Sukuna to ask him a bold&nbsp;
question in itself. He was strong, right?

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:11.800
Powering up as if it's his last chance, Kashimo&nbsp;
unleashes waves of electricity that shoot out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:16.840
in every direction. Undeterred by the power&nbsp;
increase, Sukuna catches Kashimo off-guard and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:21.200
appears right behind him, grabbing his hands&nbsp;
and pummeling him with the two free ones.

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.280
Coughing up blood now, Sukuna slams him&nbsp;
to the ground and throws the demonstrably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:30.440
weaker sorcerer across the decimated landscape&nbsp;
of Shinjuku. Pulling up his hand in preparation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:35.080
for his next cursed electricity blast,&nbsp;
Kashimo is left stunned. In front of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:39.760
him now and with seemingly no escape,&nbsp;
a bunch of world-slashing dismantles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:45.240
all overlapping to form a net, rush&nbsp;
forth like a torrential wave of death.

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:50.880
Flashing away to a place that probably feels&nbsp;
more like home than anything for Kashimo, he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:56.400
hears someone speaking some wise words behind him.&nbsp;
Many of the world's strongest fighters must have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:02.080
challenged him. Still, with all of their strength&nbsp;
and spiritual dominance, they never cursed him in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:07.360
death. In actuality, it's more that they just&nbsp;
wanted recognition from him. Then that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:12.480
give them an understanding of what they are truly&nbsp;
worth. Yet, he butchered every last one of them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:17.560
all while simultaneously wondering how he was&nbsp;
to properly care for others. In the eyes of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:23.280
wise Sukuna, if that isn't loving-kindness,&nbsp;
then what else could it even be? He knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:28.240
that most people love them for the strength&nbsp;
they possess, then they respond to that love.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:33.920
Speaking up now and wondering if Sukuna's&nbsp;
satisfied, Kashimo asks if that is the case,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:38.360
then queries why did he decide to divide&nbsp;
his soul and move through time as a cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:44.080
object. Understanding this, Sukuna just tells&nbsp;
him that love is worthless. Through life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:48.360
he's never needed anyone to satisfy him.&nbsp;
He eats when he wants and plays with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:52.200
whatever amuses him. He lives&nbsp;
life as it befits his nature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:56.560
and if no one is able to get that through&nbsp;
their thick noggins, that's their problem.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:12:01.480
Chuckling with Sukuna’s explanation,&nbsp;
Kashimo just asks him if it ever gets old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:06.560
but is quickly told that it doesn't. Every&nbsp;
human has a unique and exuberant taste,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:11.480
which makes devouring them a perfect way&nbsp;
to pass the time until death arrives.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:16.120
I want to point out that, unlike when Gojo&nbsp;
died, Kashimo wasn't surrounded by all his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:25.440
loved friends and family, just Sukuna.&nbsp;
Kinda reminded me of the Jogoat death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:30.240
moment with just how quickly he was living then&nbsp;
in the shadow realm. Wish we got to see more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:37.400
but this is realistic; thinking Kashimo was going&nbsp;
to last even a third as long as Gojo is nuts.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:42.560
Either way, and back in reality now with Hakari’s&nbsp;
Domain shattering, Sukuna turns to see a certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:48.000
someone arriving on the battlefield. Dropping&nbsp;
in from the sky, both Yuji and Higuruma ready&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:53.360
themselves to face off against the strongest&nbsp;
entity in the history of Jujutsu Kaisen.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:58.480
This is going to be hella interesting. No idea&nbsp;
what Yuji has in store for us with his new cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:03.960
technique or whatever it is, and Sukuna is on&nbsp;
the same page, wondering what the hell he's gonna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:09.480
do here. I don't want to see Higuruma close the&nbsp;
series out by sticking Sukuna on death row; that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:13.640
just doesn't feel right to me, especially after&nbsp;
the dude managed to get around Gojo’s infinity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:17.920
I'm curious about your thoughts on everything&nbsp;
below. Did you want to see more from Kashimo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:26.960
or did you expect his final technique to be a bit&nbsp;
more potent? This might be a case of an insanely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:32.440
strong technique in the wrong person, kinda like&nbsp;
when we saw Jogo display his powers for the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:40.400
time in Shibuya, which was utterly insane compared&nbsp;
to episode 7 where Gojo dunked on him. If you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.840
to see more content like this, but for a bunch&nbsp;
of different series, then make sure to hit that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:50.280
subscribe button. We're getting pretty close to&nbsp;
200k now, which is dope asf, so it'd be cool if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:55.280
we could get there by Christmas! Either way, hit&nbsp;
the like button if you enjoyed the video. For now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.280 --> 00:14:00.520
it's been your professional degenerate&nbsp;
Diavolo, and I'll see you all in a bit. Bye.

